  "notes": "Warm off-white paper background with cream panels and thin beige borders, deep teal-green sidebar and primary buttons, amber/ochre for in-progress and eyebrow labels. Distinctive narrative-first data UX: the H1 is a computed finding sentence ('41% of your files are labeled noise. 54% of those came from HR-03, the pond.') followed by plain-language explanation and evidence chips. Earthy categorical palette (ochre, sand, khaki, sage green, grey) for rejection rules is reused consistently across bars, table row swatches and legend. Settings playground previews outcome (41.0% → 34.5%, per-detector deltas) before committing, with Apply disabled until a change; 'Unapplied filter changes' pill appears in top bar and an alert dot on Settings nav after changes (live only). Steps can be freely visited but completion is gated ('Finish step 5 first')."
